# 🌡️ Smart Environmental Monitoring System

A virtual environmental monitoring project built using Arduino Uno Rev3 and a DHT22 temperature and humidity sensor. The system monitors environmental conditions and generates automatic alerts when predefined thresholds are reached.

## 📌 Project Overview

Environmental monitoring helps us understand changes in temperature and humidity. This project demonstrates how a microcontroller can collect sensor readings, process the data, and generate alerts when environmental conditions cross specified limits.

The project is developed and tested using the Wokwi online electronics simulator, without requiring physical hardware.

## ✨ Features

* 🌡️ Temperature monitoring in Celsius.
* 💧 Relative humidity monitoring in percentage.
* 🚨 High-temperature alert when temperature reaches 35°C.
* 💦 High-humidity alert when relative humidity reaches 70%.
* 🔄 Periodic sensor readings every two seconds.
* 🛡️ Basic handling of failed sensor readings.
* 💻 Serial Monitor output for real-time observation.
* 💰 Zero hardware cost using virtual simulation.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

* Arduino Uno Rev3
* DHT22 temperature and humidity sensor
