## 🔌 Circuit Connections

| DHT22 Pin  | Arduino Uno Rev3 |
| ---------- | ---------------- |
| VCC        | 5V               |
| SDA / DATA | Digital Pin 2    |
| NC         | Not connected    |
| GND        | GND              |

## ⚙️ How It Works

1. The Arduino initializes the DHT22 sensor.
2. The sensor provides temperature and humidity readings.
3. The Arduino displays the readings in the Serial Monitor.
4. If the temperature reaches or exceeds 35°C, a high-temperature alert appears.
5. If relative humidity reaches or exceeds 70%, a high-humidity alert appears.
6. The system repeats the process every two seconds.

